# Atlas Design Controls -- MCP First

The Atlas MCP server is the **single source of truth** for every
design control artefact in this repo. Local YAML files under
`design-controls/` no longer exist. Anything you read or write that
relates to a User Need, Design Input, Design Output, Verification
Test, Validation Test, Risk, or the Software Architecture Document
MUST go through the `user-atlas-design-controls` MCP server.

- Product ID: `PROD-LEO-CLINICAL-DECISION-SUPPORT-20260515-118182E4`
- MCP server: `user-atlas-design-controls`
- ID format in Atlas: 8 hex chars (e.g. `UN-8225F9E1`, `DI-D14B711F`)

## Hard rules

1. **No local design-control YAMLs.** Never create files under any
   path matching `**/design-controls/**`. Never recreate the
   `user-needs/`, `design-inputs/`, `design-outputs/`,
   `verification-tests/`, `validation-tests/`, or `risks/` folders.
   If you find one, delete it and migrate the content to Atlas.
2. **No local traceability matrix.** Use Atlas
   `get_traceability_matrix` for trace queries. The Markdown / CSV
   matrices that used to live in `design-controls/` are gone.
3. **No legacy ID format in new content.** The legacy
   `UN-LEO-AI-099`, `DI-LEO-AI-529` etc. style is read-only history.
   Every new artefact gets an Atlas dcId of the form `<TYPE>-<8 hex>`
   from the create tool.
4. **No "I will write the YAML and migrate later".** Migrate now via
   the matching `create_*` tool. The whole point of Phase 10 was to
   stop drift between Atlas and disk.
5. **Acceptance criteria, rationale, mitigations, monitoring,
   residual risk, etc. are Atlas fields.** Use the `create_*` and
   `update_*` tools, not files.

## Where things live now

| You used to look at...                              | You now call...                                           |
|-----------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| `design-controls/user-needs/UN-*.yaml`              | `get_design_control(dc_type="user_need", dc_id=...)`      |
| `design-controls/design-inputs/DI-*.yaml`           | `get_design_control(dc_type="design_input", dc_id=...)`   |
| `design-controls/design-outputs/DO-*.yaml`          | `get_design_control(dc_type="design_output", dc_id=...)`  |
| `design-controls/verification-tests/VT-*.yaml`      | `get_design_control(dc_type="verification_test", ...)`    |
| `design-controls/validation-tests/VAL-*.yaml`       | `get_design_control(dc_type="validation_test", ...)`      |
| `design-controls/risks/R-*.yaml`                    | `get_design_control(dc_type="risk", dc_id=...)`           |
| `design-controls/DC-TM-001-traceability-matrix.md`  | `get_traceability_matrix(product_id=...)`                 |
| `design-controls/DC-ARCH-001-system-architecture.md`| `get_software_architecture_document(product_id=...)`      |

Source-of-truth helpers:

- Browse / find: `search_design_controls(query=..., dc_type=...)`,
  `get_design_control_stats(product_id=...)`, `get_traceability_gaps`.
- Audit history: `compliance/atlas-migration-evidence/atlas-id-mapping.csv`
  maps every legacy `UN-LEO-AI-*` / `DI-LEO-AI-*` / etc. to its
  Atlas dcId.

## Compliance / governance docs (NOT design controls)

These still live on disk under `compliance/`:

- `compliance/policy/` -- 20 governance / regulatory docs (DPA, DPIA,
  DTAC, NDOO, SOUP, configuration management, deployment, etc.)
- `compliance/architecture-superseded/` -- the original sources for
  the Atlas SAD, kept for the audit chain. Read-only history; for
  the live architecture use `get_software_architecture_document`.
- `compliance/design-reviews/` -- design-review minutes (`DR-*.yaml`).
- `compliance/atlas-migration-evidence/` -- the Phase 1-10 migration
  ledgers and the 2026-04-19 Atlas baseline snapshot.
- `compliance/coverage-waivers.md` -- accepted residual gaps with
  owners and clearance plans.

When you need to update a policy doc under `compliance/policy/`, you
edit the file directly. When you need to update a design control,
you call the Atlas MCP.

## See also

- `atlas-vt-enforcement.mdc` -- when you write code, the DI / DO /
  Risk / VT / VAL chain must exist in Atlas first.
- `atlas-design-controls-validation.mdc` -- Atlas validates the
  schema server-side; this rule lists the local checks you still owe
  before calling a tool.

## If MCP is unavailable

- State that MCP failed and why (auth, tool-not-found, transport).
- Ask the user to fix MCP connection or approval.
- Do **not** fall back to writing YAMLs.
- Do not write a "to migrate later" file. We just deleted 1,047 of
  those.
